      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin\\left(x-2\\pi\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u-v)=\\sin u\\cos v-\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\n\nThe fixed angle has exact values\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(2\\pi\\right)=1,\\qquad \\sin\\left(2\\pi\\right)=0.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $u=x$ and $v=2\\pi$, then simplify the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin\\left(x-2\\pi\\right)&=\\sin x\\cos\\left(2\\pi\\right)-\\cos x\\sin\\left(2\\pi\\right)\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\left(1\\right)-\\cos x\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=\\sin x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
